// Transcribed mechanically from mbedtls 3.6.7 library/ecp_curves.c: P, A,
// B, G and N of each curve and the static comb tables of G, as 64-bit
// limbs, least significant first. A <curve>_T table holds X then Y of each
// point in comb order, each padded to the limb count of P. The secp*r1
// curves have no A (A = -3); the Montgomery curves keep only P and N.

